//! lotus/stereo_reverb_time.rye — ALES189: the STEREO REVERB in real time — ALES187's linked stereo Schroeder network spoken in
//! MILLISECONDS, a thin twin over it exactly as ALES188's reverb_ms is over ALES186's reverb. ALES187 carried the reverb into stereo (the
//! same comb-and-allpass bank on both channels, each channel reverbed through its own network), yet every comb and allpass delay is a count
//! of sample INDICES. A keeper names a room in TIME — the pre-delays and decays of a hall are milliseconds, not sample counts — and the one
//! missing fact is the sample rate, which ALES5's validated Clock already holds. stereo_reverb.rye's own header named this rung ("a
//! real-time stereo twin through the ALES5 clock is a later rung, exactly as stereo_echo_time followed stereo_echo"), and ALES188's mono
//! reverb_ms opened it; this is the stereo face, mirroring reverb_ms's two-bank conversion and delegating to ALES187 unchanged.
//!
//! The crux is the family's signature: THE CLOCK ADDS ONLY THE UNITS, NEVER THE AUDIO, and the SAME conversion feeds BOTH channels.
//! stereo_reverb_ms converts start_ms, count_ms, and every comb's and allpass's delay_ms ONCE through ALES5's proven clock.samples_for
//! (bounded, refusing DurationTooLong past the clip) into an index-named comb bank and allpass bank, then delegates to ALES187's
//! stereo_reverb UNCHANGED. One converted bank feeds both channels — the image held for free, each ear the same room — so the
//! millisecond-named stereo reverb lands BYTE-FOR-BYTE the same samples on each channel as the index-named stereo reverb over the converted
//! delays and span. Because samples_for is divTrunc(rate·ms, 1000), a comb or allpass delay too short to be one whole sample converts to 0,
//! which ALES187 (through ALES186's precheck) already refuses BadDelay on both channels before any write. The two bank counts are checked
//! against reverb.max_stages first (NoCombs on an empty comb bank, TooManyStages on either over-long bank) BEFORE any conversion, so the two
//! bounded stack banks always hold their stages and both channels are untouched on a bad count. It reuses ALES188's CombSpecMs / AllpassSpecMs
//! as the timed spec types, keeping one source of truth for the millisecond-named reverb stage.
//!
//! HONESTLY NOTED — inherited whole from ALES187: like the feedback echo, the flanger, and the allpass and UNLIKE the snapshot rungs, the
//! reverb reads its delayed OUTPUT through a @divTrunc recirculation, so an exact panned integer ratio does NOT survive. The image law proven
//! is therefore the identical-channel one — a centred master staying identical through the timed reverb — the sense a mix cares about.
//!
//! Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES189.
//! Design read: active-designing/20260815-095002_fill-ales189-lotus-stereo-reverb-in-real-time.md
//! Stands on: lotus/stereo_reverb.rye (ALES187) — the linked stereo reverb this speaks in real time, delegated unchanged, its
//! StereoReverbError forwarded; lotus/reverb_time.rye (ALES188) — the mono timed twin this mirrors, its CombSpecMs / AllpassSpecMs reused;
//! lotus/reverb.rye (ALES186) — the ReverbError the reverb half of this face's error set and the max_stages bound; lotus/clock.rye (ALES5) —
//! the sample clock, its samples_for converting ms to a bounded sample count; lotus/pan.rye (ALES10) — the StereoClip and its balance invariant.
//!
//! HONEST SCOPE — software only, purely LOCAL. Two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right), a validated Clock, and two bounded stack banks
//! of at most reverb.max_stages timed stages, siloed to lotus/. No new arithmetic on the audio path — the clock's own conversion into the
//! banks, then the proven stereo reverb. It changes sample VALUES only, never a length; the two channels leave balanced. The clock is a
//! samples-per-second count, not a claim about any hardware clock; the feedbacks and gains are named fractions, not room sizes in seconds. No
//! cross-channel read, no real sample rate device, no network, no keys, no funds, no real speaker.
//!
//!   env RYE_ZIG=vendor/zig-toolchain/zig rye/bin/rye run lotus/stereo_reverb_time.rye selftest

const std = @import("std");
const assert = std.debug.assert;
const print = std.debug.print;

const timeline = @import("timeline.rye");
const pan = @import("pan.rye");
const clock = @import("clock.rye");
const reverb = @import("reverb.rye");
const reverb_time = @import("reverb_time.rye");
const stereo_reverb = @import("stereo_reverb.rye");

pub const stereo_reverb_time_version = "20260815.095002";

/// The timed stereo reverb's faults are ALES5's clock edges beside ALES187's reverb edges, forwarded unchanged: DurationTooLong from the
/// clock (a span or stage delay past the clip), and NoCombs, TooManyStages, BadDelay (a converted delay being zero among them), BadGain, and
/// BadRange from the reverb. The real-time stereo face adds no fault of its own — it converts the units, then runs the proven stereo reverb.
pub const StereoReverbTimeError = clock.ClockError || reverb.ReverbError;

/// Reverberate a stereo master over a span named in MILLISECONDS: convert `start_ms`, `count_ms`, and every comb's and allpass's `delay_ms`
/// through ALES5's proven clock.samples_for (bounded, refusing DurationTooLong past the clip) into an index-named comb bank and allpass bank,
/// then delegate to ALES187's `stereo_reverb` UNCHANGED — the same linked Schroeder network on both channels, now named in real time. The
/// clock adds only the units, and the same converted bank feeds both channels, so this lands byte-for-byte the same samples on each channel
/// as the index-named stereo reverb over the converted delays and span, the image held. A stage delay too short to be one whole sample
/// converts to zero, which the reverb refuses BadDelay on both channels. The bank counts are checked against reverb.max_stages first (NoCombs
/// on an empty comb bank, TooManyStages on either over-long bank, before any conversion). Forwards ALES5's DurationTooLong and ALES187's
/// NoCombs / TooManyStages / BadDelay / BadGain / BadRange before any write; on refusal both channels are untouched and balanced. Values
/// only — never a length; reuses ALES188's CombSpecMs / AllpassSpecMs as the timed spec types.
pub fn stereo_reverb_ms(
    sc: *pan.StereoClip,
    clk: clock.Clock,
    start_ms: u32,
    count_ms: u32,
    combs_ms: []const reverb_time.CombSpecMs,
    allpasses_ms: []const reverb_time.AllpassSpecMs,
) StereoReverbTimeError!void {
    // invariant: the two channels enter balanced — the defining StereoClip invariant, the ground the shared conversion and reverb preserve.
    assert(sc.left.len == sc.right.len);
    // invariant: the clock is valid, so each conversion is bounded and safe; the units change, never the audio.
    assert(clk.rate >= 1 and clk.rate <= clock.max_rate);
    // invariant: a reverb needs at least one comb and a bounded bank on each side — checked BEFORE any conversion so the two stack banks
    // always hold their stages and both channels are untouched on a bad count. ALES187 re-validates the same bounds against the shared length.
    if (combs_ms.len == 0) return error.NoCombs;
    if (combs_ms.len > reverb.max_stages) return error.TooManyStages;
    if (allpasses_ms.len > reverb.max_stages) return error.TooManyStages;

    // Convert each timed comb into an index-named CombSpec in a bounded stack bank — the delay through the clock, the feedback unchanged.
    var comb_buf: [reverb.max_stages]reverb.CombSpec = undefined;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < combs_ms.len) : (i += 1) {
        const c = combs_ms[i];
        const delay = try clock.samples_for(clk, c.delay_ms);
        comb_buf[i] = .{ .delay = delay, .fb_num = c.fb_num, .fb_den = c.fb_den };
    }

    // Convert each timed allpass into an index-named AllpassSpec in a bounded stack bank — the delay through the clock, the gain unchanged.
    var allpass_buf: [reverb.max_stages]reverb.AllpassSpec = undefined;
    var j: u32 = 0;
    while (j < allpasses_ms.len) : (j += 1) {
        const a = allpasses_ms[j];
        const delay = try clock.samples_for(clk, a.delay_ms);
        allpass_buf[j] = .{ .delay = delay, .num = a.num, .den = a.den };
    }

    const start = try clock.samples_for(clk, start_ms);
    const count = try clock.samples_for(clk, count_ms);
    // invariant: exactly the given stages were converted, each within its buffer bound.
    assert(i == combs_ms.len and i <= comb_buf.len);
    assert(j == allpasses_ms.len and j <= allpass_buf.len);
    // The stereo reverb is ALES187's, unchanged — one converted bank feeding both channels, each reverberating its OWN audio. A zero
    // converted delay is refused BadDelay there, both channels untouched.
    try stereo_reverb.stereo_reverb(sc, start, count, comb_buf[0..combs_ms.len], allpass_buf[0..allpasses_ms.len]);

    // invariant: the channels leave balanced — a timed reverb writes values only, so each channel holds its starting length and the image stays aligned in time.
    assert(sc.left.len == sc.right.len);
    assert(sc.left.len <= sc.left.buf.len and sc.right.len <= sc.right.buf.len);
}

// --- selftest: THE CLOCK-ADDS-ONLY-UNITS LAW — at 1 sample/ms both channels equal ALES187's index-named stereo reverb byte for byte; THE
//     REAL-RATE LAW — at 48 kHz 1 ms == 48 samples on both, the first recirculation there; THE IDENTICAL-CHANNEL IMAGE LAW — a centred master
//     stays identical; THE FORWARDING / ATOMICITY / BALANCE LAW — a sub-sample comb, a long stage delay, an empty bank, a unity feedback, an
//     out-of-range span each refusing by name with both channels untouched and balanced, count_ms 0 the identity ---------------------------

fn eq(got: []const i16, want: []const i16) bool {
    if (got.len != want.len) return false;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < want.len) : (i += 1) if (got[i] != want[i]) return false;
    return true;
}

fn load_stereo(sc: *pan.StereoClip, l: []const i16, r: []const i16) !void {
    try timeline.splice(&sc.left, 0, l);
    try timeline.splice(&sc.right, 0, r);
}

fn run_selftest() !u8 {
    // 1. THE CLOCK-ADDS-ONLY-UNITS LAW — at 1 sample per ms, a timed stereo reverb lands byte-for-byte the same samples on BOTH channels as
    //    ALES187's index-named stereo reverb over the converted delays and span, with genuinely different per-channel content. Run both tools
    //    side by side and demand equality: stereo_reverb_ms adds no arithmetic on the audio path.
    {
        const c = try clock.make(1000); // 1 sample per ms — a millisecond equals a sample, legible on a bench
        const ll = [_]i16{ 8000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
        const rr = [_]i16{ 0, 0, 6000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
        const combs_ms = [_]reverb_time.CombSpecMs{
            .{ .delay_ms = 2, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 },
            .{ .delay_ms = 3, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 3 },
        };
        const allpasses_ms = [_]reverb_time.AllpassSpecMs{.{ .delay_ms = 2, .num = 1, .den = 2 }};

        var timed = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&timed, &ll, &rr);
        try stereo_reverb_ms(&timed, c, 0, 8, &combs_ms, &allpasses_ms);

        var indexed = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&indexed, &ll, &rr);
        const combs = [_]reverb.CombSpec{
            .{ .delay = 2, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 },
            .{ .delay = 3, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 3 },
        };
        const allpasses = [_]reverb.AllpassSpec{.{ .delay = 2, .num = 1, .den = 2 }};
        try stereo_reverb.stereo_reverb(&indexed, 0, 8, &combs, &allpasses);

        if (!eq(timed.left.samples(), indexed.left.samples())) return error.LeftNotSameAsIndexed;
        if (!eq(timed.right.samples(), indexed.right.samples())) return error.RightNotSameAsIndexed;
        // the two channels genuinely differ — the left is not the right rung, proving no crossing
        if (eq(timed.left.samples(), timed.right.samples())) return error.ChannelsDidNotDiffer;
    }

    // 2. THE REAL-RATE LAW — at 48 kHz, 1 ms converts to divTrunc(48000·1, 1000) = 48 samples on both channels. A single comb at delay_ms 1
    //    (no allpass — a comb alone is ALES66's echo) over a clip long enough lands its first recirculation exactly 48 samples after the
    //    impulse on each channel, matching the index-named stereo reverb at delay 48. Proven by equality and by reading the tap position.
    {
        const c = try clock.make(48000);
        if (clock.samples_for(c, 1) catch 0 != 48) return error.RateConversionWrong; // guard the arithmetic itself
        var lbuf: [240]i16 = [_]i16{0} ** 240; // 240 samples == 5 ms at 48 kHz, so count_ms 5 covers the whole clip exactly
        var rbuf: [240]i16 = [_]i16{0} ** 240;
        lbuf[0] = 10000; // an impulse at index 0 on the left
        rbuf[0] = 6000; //  a different impulse on the right, so the channels genuinely differ
        const combs_ms = [_]reverb_time.CombSpecMs{.{ .delay_ms = 1, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 }};
        const none = [_]reverb_time.AllpassSpecMs{};

        var timed = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&timed, &lbuf, &rbuf);
        try stereo_reverb_ms(&timed, c, 0, 5, &combs_ms, &none); // span 5 ms == 240 samples, 1 ms delay == 48 samples, fb 1/2

        var indexed = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&indexed, &lbuf, &rbuf);
        const combs = [_]reverb.CombSpec{.{ .delay = 48, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 }};
        const noneidx = [_]reverb.AllpassSpec{};
        try stereo_reverb.stereo_reverb(&indexed, 0, 240, &combs, &noneidx);
        if (!eq(timed.left.samples(), indexed.left.samples())) return error.RealRateLeftNotSameAsIndexed;
        if (!eq(timed.right.samples(), indexed.right.samples())) return error.RealRateRightNotSameAsIndexed;
        // the first recirculation sits at index 48, half the impulse, on each channel
        if (timed.left.samples()[48] != 5000) return error.LeftTapNotAtConvertedDelay;
        if (timed.right.samples()[48] != 3000) return error.RightTapNotAtConvertedDelay;
    }

    // 3. THE IDENTICAL-CHANNEL IMAGE LAW — a centred master (both channels equal) stays identical through the timed reverb: the same
    //    conversion, then the same deterministic network on each channel. Honestly noted (inherited from ALES187): an exact panned ratio does
    //    NOT survive the @divTrunc recirculation, so only the centred image is claimed.
    {
        const c = try clock.make(1000);
        const same = [_]i16{ 8000, -3000, 0, 2000, 0, 0, -1000, 0 };
        const combs_ms = [_]reverb_time.CombSpecMs{
            .{ .delay_ms = 2, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 },
            .{ .delay_ms = 3, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 3 },
        };
        const allpasses_ms = [_]reverb_time.AllpassSpecMs{.{ .delay_ms = 2, .num = 1, .den = 2 }};
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &same, &same);
        try stereo_reverb_ms(&sc, c, 0, 8, &combs_ms, &allpasses_ms);
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), sc.right.samples())) return error.IdentityChannelsSplit;
    }

    // 4. A SUB-SAMPLE COMB REFUSES BadDelay — at 1 sample per ms a comb delay of 0 ms converts to 0 samples, which the reverb refuses on
    //    both channels; the timed face forwards it by name rather than silently doing nothing, both channels untouched and balanced.
    {
        const c = try clock.make(1000);
        const tl = [_]i16{ 5, -6, 7, -8 };
        const tr = [_]i16{ -7, 6, -5, 4 };
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &tl, &tr);
        const combs_ms = [_]reverb_time.CombSpecMs{.{ .delay_ms = 0, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 }};
        const none = [_]reverb_time.AllpassSpecMs{};
        if (stereo_reverb_ms(&sc, c, 0, 4, &combs_ms, &none)) |_| return error.SubSampleSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadDelay) return error.WrongSubSample;
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(sc.right.samples(), &tr) or sc.left.len != sc.right.len) return error.SubSampleRefusalMutated;
    }

    // 5. A STAGE DELAY PAST THE CLIP REFUSES DurationTooLong — an allpass delay_ms whose sample count exceeds max_clip is refused by the
    //    clock's own bound during conversion, before any write, both channels untouched and balanced. A valid comb sits ahead of it, so the
    //    fault forwards from the allpass conversion, not only the first stage.
    {
        const c = try clock.make(1000);
        const tl = [_]i16{ 1, 2, 3 };
        const tr = [_]i16{ 3, 2, 1 };
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &tl, &tr);
        const combs_ms = [_]reverb_time.CombSpecMs{.{ .delay_ms = 1, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 }};
        const long = [_]reverb_time.AllpassSpecMs{.{ .delay_ms = timeline.max_clip + 1, .num = 1, .den = 2 }};
        if (stereo_reverb_ms(&sc, c, 0, 3, &combs_ms, &long)) |_| return error.LongDelaySlipped else |e| if (e != error.DurationTooLong) return error.WrongLongDelay;
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(sc.right.samples(), &tr) or sc.left.len != sc.right.len) return error.LongDelayRefusalMutated;
    }

    // 6. THE REVERB'S BANK FAULTS FORWARD — an empty comb bank refuses NoCombs (before any conversion), a feedback at unity refuses BadGain,
    //    and an out-of-range span refuses BadRange, each by name with both channels untouched and balanced; and count_ms = 0 is the identity.
    {
        const c = try clock.make(1000);
        const tl = [_]i16{ 1, 2, 3 };
        const tr = [_]i16{ 3, 2, 1 };
        const none = [_]reverb_time.AllpassSpecMs{};

        var n = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&n, &tl, &tr);
        const nocombs = [_]reverb_time.CombSpecMs{};
        if (stereo_reverb_ms(&n, c, 0, 3, &nocombs, &none)) |_| return error.NoCombsSlipped else |e| if (e != error.NoCombs) return error.WrongNoCombs;
        if (!eq(n.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(n.right.samples(), &tr) or n.left.len != n.right.len) return error.NoCombsRefusalMutated;

        var g = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&g, &tl, &tr);
        const unity = [_]reverb_time.CombSpecMs{.{ .delay_ms = 1, .fb_num = 4, .fb_den = 4 }};
        if (stereo_reverb_ms(&g, c, 0, 3, &unity, &none)) |_| return error.UnityFbSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadGain) return error.WrongUnityFb;
        if (!eq(g.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(g.right.samples(), &tr) or g.left.len != g.right.len) return error.UnityFbRefusalMutated;

        var d = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&d, &tl, &tr);
        const good = [_]reverb_time.CombSpecMs{.{ .delay_ms = 1, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 }};
        if (stereo_reverb_ms(&d, c, 2, 5, &good, &none)) |_| return error.BadRangeSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadRange) return error.WrongBadRange; // start 2 ms + count 5 ms > len 3
        if (!eq(d.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(d.right.samples(), &tr) or d.left.len != d.right.len) return error.RangeRefusalMutated;

        var noop = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&noop, &[_]i16{ 8000, -8000, 4000 }, &[_]i16{ -50, 60, -70 });
        try stereo_reverb_ms(&noop, c, 1, 0, &good, &none); // empty span — identity
        if (!eq(noop.left.samples(), &[_]i16{ 8000, -8000, 4000 })) return error.ZeroCountLeftChanged;
        if (!eq(noop.right.samples(), &[_]i16{ -50, 60, -70 })) return error.ZeroCountRightChanged;
    }

    print("GREEN ales-stereo-reverb-time: the STEREO REVERB IN REAL TIME — ALES187's linked stereo Schroeder network spoken in " ++
        "MILLISECONDS, a thin twin over it exactly as ALES188's reverb_ms is over ALES186's reverb. The clock adds only the units, never " ++
        "the audio, and the SAME conversion feeds BOTH channels: stereo_reverb_ms converts start_ms, count_ms, and every comb's and " ++
        "allpass's delay_ms once through ALES5's samples_for into an index-named comb bank and allpass bank and delegates to ALES187's " ++
        "stereo_reverb unchanged, so a millisecond-named stereo reverb lands BYTE-FOR-BYTE the same samples on each channel as the " ++
        "index-named stereo reverb over the converted delays and span (the grounding law, both tools run, the channels genuinely " ++
        "differing). At 48 kHz, 1 ms converts to 48 samples on both channels and the first recirculation sits exactly there on each; an " ++
        "identical-channel master stays identical through the timed reverb (an exact panned ratio does NOT survive the @divTrunc " ++
        "recirculation, inherited from ALES187). A sub-sample comb (0 ms) refuses BadDelay rather than silently doing nothing; a stage " ++
        "delay past the clip refuses DurationTooLong; an empty comb bank refuses NoCombs, a feedback at unity BadGain, an out-of-range " ++
        "span BadRange, each leaving BOTH channels untouched and balanced; count_ms = 0 the identity on both. No new arithmetic on the " ++
        "audio path — the clock's own conversion into the banks, then the proven stereo reverb; two bounded i16 Clips and a validated " ++
        "clock, siloed to lotus/; no cross-channel read, no real sample rate device, no network, no keys, no funds, no real speaker\n", .{});
    return 0;
}

pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !u8 {
    _ = init;
    return run_selftest();
}
